note for test at the latch on a byte counter (type 6, the smallest signed type) that the body makes negative
note (B.LT, not B.LO): the first pass sets i to -5, so i = 0, -4 .. 2 runs 8 passes (exit 8); an unsigned
note latch test leaves after 1 pass. frneg pins the same choice for long (type 9).
om2
fn main to int
n = long 0
for i byte 3
if eq n 0
i = sub i 5
end
n = add n 1
end
ret int n
end
